# ==============================================================================
# pulsaros profile — base package list (Phase 2 of engine/build-iso.sh)
# One package per line, '#' comments ignored. This is what goes into the
# dnf --installroot base-cache bootstrap: a plain Fedora GNOME system,
# with no Pulsar OS / ParchaOS branding/apps yet (those come from
# PROFILE_REPO_PACKAGES in packages.sh, installed against the profile's
# own COPR in Phase 5). Keeping this list unbranded is what lets Phase
# 1's "get a plain Fedora GNOME live ISO building before any branding"
# checkpoint actually mean something — same pattern the KDE (pearos)
# profile used successfully.
#
# Adapted directly from profiles/pearos/packages.list — see that file's
# own comments for the real bugs already found and fixed in the shared
# non-DE-specific parts (btrfs-progs/cracklib-dicts/squashfs-tools for
# Calamares, mesa-vulkan-drivers/microcode_ctl for AMD+Intel GPU/CPU
# support, grub2/shim for boot). Only the desktop-environment-specific
# packages below actually changed.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Core system ---
fedora-release
dnf
systemd
systemd-udev
systemd-pam
NetworkManager
kernel-core
kernel-modules
kernel-modules-extra
linux-firmware
dracut
dracut-live

# --- Hardware support (AMD + Intel, see pearos profile's own comment
# for the real gaps this was found to close) ---
mesa-vulkan-drivers
microcode_ctl
grub2-pc-modules
grub2-efi-x64-cdboot
grub2-efi-x64-modules
shim-x64
mokutil
sudo
passwd
util-linux
procps-ng
bash-completion
polkit
dbus-broker

# --- Live-media specifics ---
livesys-scripts
plymouth
plymouth-theme-spinner

# Installer (Calamares, same as the KDE profile — Fedora ships it
# directly, no COPR/build needed).
calamares

# Calamares partition/users/unpackfs module dependencies — same three
# real bugs already found/fixed once in the KDE profile (see its
# packages.list comments for the exact failure modes): mkfs.btrfs,
# password dictionary validation, and unsquashfs all need explicit
# packages Fedora doesn't pull in by default.
btrfs-progs
cracklib-dicts
squashfs-tools

# --- GNOME desktop ---
# GNOME Shell is Wayland-native. Real bug found via a real dnf query
# (2026-09-22): unlike the KDE profile's kwin-x11 fallback, Fedora 44 no
# longer ships a separate "gnome-session-xsession" Xorg-fallback
# subpackage at all (confirmed via `dnf repoquery '*gnome-session*'` —
# only gnome-session and gnome-session-wayland-session exist) — dropped
# rather than guessing at a different name; GNOME on Xorg isn't a
# priority for this project anyway (Wayland-only, same as the KDE
# profile's own real-world default).
gnome-shell
gnome-session
gnome-session-wayland-session
gnome-control-center
gdm
xdg-desktop-portal-gnome
xdg-desktop-portal
gnome-keyring
# Real bug avoided (2026-09-23): not confirmed as a transitive
# dependency of gnome-shell via `dnf repoquery --requires` -- adding
# explicitly since customize.sh's dconf-based extension-enablement
# mechanism needs the `dconf` CLI at build time (Phase 5.5).
dconf
gnome-shell-extension-common
gnome-disk-utility
gnome-system-monitor
gnome-firmware
NetworkManager-adsl

# --- Apps referenced by Pulsar OS's / pearOS's default app set (Fedora
# equivalents for now — Pulsar OS's own forks like the patched Nautilus
# and Sayri come from this profile's own COPR once ported, see
# packages.sh, same pattern as pafari/pearos-dock in the KDE profile) ---
# nautilus deliberately NOT listed here (2026-09-23) -- parchaos-finder
# (Parcher, packages.sh) Obsoletes/Conflicts/Provides it directly, same
# drop-in-replacement pattern as the real Pulsar OS package itself.
gnome-terminal
gnome-text-editor
loupe
file-roller
gnome-screenshot
gnome-calculator
gnome-weather
gnome-calendar
gnome-contacts

# AirDrop/Handoff equivalent — GSConnect, a real GNOME Shell extension
# (confirmed listed in Pulsar OS's own bundled-extensions table,
# andyholmes/gnome-shell-extension-gsconnect upstream). Fedora ships it
# directly.
gnome-shell-extension-gsconnect

# macOS-style trackpad gestures — same real Fedora package the KDE
# profile uses (touchegg, DE-agnostic system-level daemon); config
# still needs porting/verifying for GNOME's own gesture conventions.
touchegg

# --- Fonts / basics needed for the branding layer to render correctly ---
google-noto-sans-fonts
google-noto-emoji-fonts

# Real bug found via the first real branded build attempt (2026-09-23):
# customize.sh's flathub remote-add step failed with "execv(flatpak)
# failed: No such file or directory" -- flatpak was never added to
# this profile's own package list at all (present in the KDE profile's
# packages.list, missed when adapting it for GNOME).
flatpak
